"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The budget was later increased to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and real-time analytics integration. The project team expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, joining in an onboarding session on September 10th. In July, the team gathered ideas to leverage AI for data visualization, with proposals due by July 20th. The project reached a significant milestone with the successful completion of the testing phase and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype, ahead of schedule. A compliance plan budget of $55,000 was approved for training and audits, and a separate $15,000 budget was approved for specialized coding and project management training. A celebration for the milestone is scheduled for October 10th, with the next phase focusing on user interface enhancements commencing in October."
